 "title": "Low DO and High DO Conditions in Genome-Wide Analysis",
 "summary": "This cluster is about the comparison of Low DO and High DO conditions in genome-wide base substitution analysis. The Low DO condition is associated with various processes, including protein synthesis, sulfur metabolism, and ribosome biogenesis. It is also enriched in Cytoplasmic translation and causes ROS pressure. The High DO condition is associated with several methods, including C > A, C > G, C > T, T > A, T > C, and T > G. The Genome-Wide Base Substitution Analysis is involved in these conditions and identifies Mismatch-rate and candidate variant-rate analyses.",
